INT. PEDIATRIC WARD - NIGHT

Dim corridor. Cartoon murals peeling. The hum of a vending machine.

A MAN in scrubs and a hospital badge pushes a gurney. Face tired. Badge reads D. VANTERPOOL.

NURSE PHILOMENA ACHEBE-LINDQVIST, 30s, jogs after him.

PHILOMENA
Doctor, wait.

MAN
Not now.

PHILOMENA
She's coding.

MAN
Which room?

PHILOMENA
Seven.

They sprint. The gurney squeaks.

INT. ROOM SEVEN - CONTINUOUS

A small girl, five, on the bed, tiny chest still. Monitors scream. Her mother is not present.

The Man leans in. Starts compressions with two fingers.

MAN
Epi!

PHILOMENA
Pushing!

MAN
Again!

The monitor spikes. Then another tracing. The girl gasps.

PHILOMENA
She's back.

The Man wilts. Wipes his forehead with his sleeve.

A woman in a coat bursts through the door, wild-eyed. MRS. ODALYS ABERNATHY-FENWICK, 30s, the girl's mother.

ODALYS
Is she--

MAN
She's breathing.

ODALYS
Thank you. Thank God. Thank you, Dr. Vanterpool.

The Man closes his eyes.

VANTERPOOL
I'm not a doctor.

ODALYS
What?

VANTERPOOL
I'm the night janitor.

PHILOMENA
(whisper)
Don Vanterpool. He's been here twenty years.

ODALYS
But you saved her.

VANTERPOOL
I watched the doctors. For twenty years.

Silence. Odalys takes his hand in both of hers. Philomena looks at him as if seeing him for the first time.

VANTERPOOL (CONT'D)
Somebody had to start.
